(*The result above is a form that still has to be integrated over the moduli s\
pace of the 4-punctured sphere. \
Adding such integrations to StringCode is W.I.P.*)

Future directions - Konishi brackets

In[16]:= (*We can also define string fields at different massive levels. Here, \
we define ghost number +2 string fields at mass level one. \
These are precisely the string fields we must consider if we want to compute t\
he Konishi mass from SFT.*)

mass1dX[F_, \[Mu]1_, \[Nu]1_, \[Mu]2_, \[Nu]2_, z_, zbar_] := 
  R[ProfileX[F[\[Mu]1, \[Nu]1, \[Mu]2, \[Nu]2], {}, z, zbar], c[0, z], 
   ct[0, zbar], exp\[Phi]f[-1, z], \[Psi][\[Mu]1, 0, z], dX[\[Nu]1, 0, z], 
   exp\[Phi]tf[-1, zbar], \[Psi]t[\[Mu]2, 0, zbar], dXt[\[Nu]2, 0, zbar]];


(*BRST action mass-level 1 correction*)

In[20]:= (actBRST[mass1dX[Kon, \[Rho]1, \[Sigma]1, \[Rho]2, \[Sigma]2, z, zbar]]) //. 
    derAppend // canonicalizeDummies // ContractDelta // Simplify

